<decompilertest>
<!--
    On arm64e the blended modifier of a hidden pointer signing was printed as
    the next call's first argument.  clang builds the modifier in x8 and
    moves it to x16:

      mov x8,x19; movk x8,#0xaea0,lsl #48; mov x16,x8; pacda x17,x16

    AARCH64.pspec leaves ShowPAC at 0, so `pacda x17,x16` lifts to a copy of
    x17 and does not read x16.  The value in x8 then has one reader left, the
    call that follows, and x8 is the `hiddenret` input entry of
    AARCH64_apple.cspec: trial scoring made it active and it sorted ahead of
    x0, so a three-argument call printed four.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring" (kuna_hiddenretarg.rs,
    always on).  On arm64e a value whose bits 48..55 are known and are neither
    all clear nor all set is not an address, so it is not a result buffer and
    the trial is rescored no-use.

    clang -target arm64e-apple-ios16.0, hand-written; `swap` is outside the
    image, so its body proves nothing:

      swap_signed  ldr x17,[x0]; mov x8,x19; movk x8,#0xaea0,lsl #48;
                   mov x16,x8; pacda x17,x16; mov x1,x17; mov x0,#0;
                   mov x2,x19; bl swap
      swap_global  the same with x9 = adr slot in place of x19, so the
                   modifier folds to the constant 0xaea0000000100100
      tagged       mov x8,x1; movk x8,#0xae00,lsl #48; mov x0,#7; bl swap
                   the control: bits 48..55 are clear, a tagged address
      buffer       add x8,sp,#8; mov x0,#7; bl swap; ldr x0,[sp,#8]
                   the control: a real result buffer

    Before the fix swap_signed printed
    `swap(a1 & 0xffffffffffff | 0xaea0000000000000,0,*a0,a1)` and swap_global
    `swap(0xaea0000000100100,0,*a0,0x100100)`.
-->
